  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream/main a6bd69d8).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Viewport box select** (`crates/ui/src/box_pick.rs`, `egui_app/shell.rs`): Ctrl (or Shift) + left drag in Edge or Face mode, with an operation open and no other pick draft collecting, draws a rubber band instead of orbiting. On release it adds every visible feature edge chain (Edge mode) or welded face (Face mode) in the box to the operation's picks, as **one `SetOperationGeometry`**, so it is one undo step. A drag to the right is a **window** (takes only what lies wholly inside), a drag to the left is a **crossing** box (also takes what it touches). The band is solid for a window and dashed for a crossing box. A plain left drag still orbits.\n- **The rule** (`crates/app/src/pick/box_pick.rs`: `box_bodies`, `box_select`, `box_select_top`) follows #692's one pick rule. Only feature chains are candidates (never facet seams). A candidate counts only if part of it is unoccluded from the eye, using the click pick's own sight test (`feature_pick::occluded`, now `pub(super)`, with no behaviour change), at most 16 sight rays per candidate. Pick-through stays off. Only parts are candidates, never stock or fixtures, but stock and fixtures still hide what lies behind them.\n- **MCP**: new tool `pick_in_box` (`crates/app/src/mcp/box_pick.rs`). It takes a world X/Y box seen from straight above (the Top view, orthographic), with `mode` window/crossing and `kind` chains/faces. By default it adds to the current picks; `replace: true` replaces them. One undo step. An empty, degenerate or already-picked box is refused with a message that names the reason. `mcp::pick::kind_door` is now `pub(super)` so the new tool can reuse it.\n- The Selection row's hover text documents the gesture. Decisions are in `docs/decisions/979-box-select-picks.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/box_pick.rs` uses a 100 x 60 x 10 plate with two square through-cutouts:\n  - `a_window_around_one_cutout_takes_exactly_its_top_rim`: from the top in ortho, exactly the cutout's 4 top-rim chains. In perspective, straight over the hole, the eye sees into it, so the result is 12 chains, all on that cutout.\n  - `a_window_around_everything_takes_every_top_rim_chain_and_no_hidden_one`: 12 top-rim chains (outer + 2 cutouts), all at the top. Pick-through gives 36 (the hidden ones exist). Seen from below, only the bottom rims.\n  - `a_crossing_box_takes_what_it_touches_a_window_only_what_it_holds`\n  - `faces_box_the_same_way_and_hidden_faces_stay_out`\n  - `degenerate_boxes_take_nothing`\n  - `mcp_pick_in_box_adds_the_rim_in_one_undo_step`: covers two boxes and two undos, `replace`, and refusals.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/box_select.rs` drives real egui pointer and modifier events on the seeded shell with the plate imported, Top view, ortho:\n  - `a_ctrl_drag_window_around_one_cutout_adds_its_rim_in_one_undo_step`: no orbit, exactly 4 chains appended to Contour1, and one Undo restores the seed's pick.\n  - `a_right_to_left_drag_is_a_crossing_box_and_a_plain_drag_still_orbits`\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green on 6716fad1 (app suites 27 s incl. box_pick, feature_pick, mcp_pick; ui lib + 10 suites 17 s)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real-window (winit/wgpu) look of the rubber band. Only the kittest harness drew it. No snapshot PNG changed.\n- The user's actual cutouts project from #241. It is not in the repo, so the plate fixture stands in for it.\n- Very large meshes: the cost is up to 16 sight rays per in-box candidate, each against every facet. It was not timed on a 1M-facet model.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill's tool table is not updated, because it is a process file and would need a PROCESS_VERSION bump. `tools/list` carries the new tool's description and schema.\n\nChangelog: Viewport box select - Ctrl+drag in Edge/Face mode adds every visible edge chain or face in the box to the open operation's picks in one undo step (drag right: window, left: crossing); MCP `pick_in_box` does the same from the Top view (#979)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #979\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
